# Downloaded dictionary sources ARE committed — see D-41 and the phase-01
# progress notes. Three of the four have no version history and a past version
# cannot be re-fetched, so committing them is what makes a shipped build
# reproducible and a fresh clone self-contained. ~30 MB, refreshed once or
# twice a year.
*.part

# Build output
tools/dictbuild/data/build/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Android / Gradle
# NOTE: gradle/wrapper/ and gradlew* ARE committed on purpose — the wrapper is
# what makes a fresh clone build with the right Gradle and nothing installed
# globally. Only build output and machine-local paths are ignored.
.gradle/
build/
local.properties
*.apk
*.aab
*.iml
.idea/
.cxx/
captures/

# Third-party test images, used for measurement and never committed.
#
# Photographs and scans found online are invaluable for tuning the scan
# geometry — real typesetting, real perspective, real lighting — but their
# licensing is unknown and this repository is public. They are therefore
# treated as strictly local: dropped in fixtures-raw/, processed into
# probe-prefixed assets so an instrumented test can read them, measured, and
# deleted. What survives is the *numbers* in docs/ and any fixture we generate
# ourselves to match them (tools/fixtures/make_fixtures.py).
#
# The `probe-` prefix is load-bearing: it is what keeps `git add -A` from
# sweeping a third-party image into a public repository's permanent history.
# Committed fixtures are named sign-* (generated) or photo-* (ours by right).
/fixtures-raw/
/app/src/androidTest/assets/probe-*
# The scratch probe that reads them. Disposable; must not outlive the images.
/app/src/androidTest/kotlin/com/spotterkanji/app/scan/FixtureProbeTest.kt
